WEBVTT

00:26.735 --> 00:29.070
You said you'd never pick up a gun again.

00:30.905 --> 00:32.115
So why join the police?

00:34.826 --> 00:36.244
I believe there are ways

00:37.037 --> 00:40.165
to protect people without using a gun.

00:43.752 --> 00:44.878
I see.

00:46.129 --> 00:47.172
Welcome.

00:47.255 --> 00:49.215
Captain, shall we head inside?

00:50.008 --> 00:50.842
Come on in.

00:53.011 --> 00:54.763
This is Officer Seo Jae-hui,

00:55.472 --> 00:57.766
Lieutenant Ahn Ji-wan,
and Inspector Oh Dae-han.

01:02.854 --> 01:04.022
I said piss off!

01:04.898 --> 01:07.942
You're killing my damn buzz,
for fuck's sake.

01:08.443 --> 01:11.071
What the hell does your daughter's death

01:12.405 --> 01:14.282
have to do with us?

01:14.866 --> 01:17.285
I came here
after identifying my daughter's body.

01:18.661 --> 01:20.789
Don't you dare insult my daughter's death.

01:20.872 --> 01:22.040
Cut the bullshit.

01:22.123 --> 01:24.417
Get this old man's mug out of here.

01:24.501 --> 01:25.877
So what? Huh?

01:25.960 --> 01:27.670
What do you want from us?

01:27.754 --> 01:30.548
What do you want? Did we kill her?

01:30.632 --> 01:33.468
So why the hell
are you crashing our party?

01:33.551 --> 01:34.719
Did I fucking kill her?

01:34.803 --> 01:37.013
What do you want from us?

01:37.847 --> 01:40.266
Apologize at my daughter's funeral.

01:40.850 --> 01:44.437
Apologize?
Did your daughter ask you to do this?

01:45.396 --> 01:48.024
Unless you wanna join your daughter
in the morgue,

01:48.775 --> 01:50.985
just shut the fuck up
and piss off, motherfucker.

01:51.069 --> 01:52.487
Who's the old guy?

01:52.570 --> 01:53.404
I said piss off.

01:53.488 --> 01:54.989
Don't fucking mind it.

01:55.073 --> 01:56.908
- Piss off.
- It's pissing me off.

01:56.991 --> 01:59.077
I said piss off, you fucking son of a--

02:10.130 --> 02:11.589
Where the fuck are you going?

02:14.050 --> 02:14.926
Damn it.

02:16.136 --> 02:18.138
What the fuck? That bastard is crazy!

02:18.221 --> 02:19.347
Someone died…

02:21.141 --> 02:23.518
yet you people don't feel any guilt.

02:25.728 --> 02:27.522
There is no hope left for you.

02:28.439 --> 02:31.067
Please don't kill me.

02:31.151 --> 02:32.026
Please…

02:32.735 --> 02:33.778
What?

02:34.362 --> 02:35.613
Please spare me.

02:36.114 --> 02:37.365
- Please.
- Sir.

02:37.866 --> 02:40.285
Please spare me this once. I…

02:40.785 --> 02:43.413
Please just spare me this once. Sir.

02:43.913 --> 02:45.290
Just this once!

02:45.790 --> 02:47.667
Please spare me.

02:47.750 --> 02:49.169
Please, I'm begging you.

02:50.211 --> 02:51.296
Why didn't you…

02:54.340 --> 02:56.092
spare my daughter?

02:57.844 --> 02:59.220
You fucking bastard!

02:59.888 --> 03:00.722
Out of my way.

03:17.488 --> 03:18.573
- Excuse me. A gun.
- Hey.

03:18.656 --> 03:20.074
- What?
- A crazy bastard. A gun.

03:20.158 --> 03:21.534
There's a gun.

03:22.035 --> 03:23.077
A gun.

03:25.788 --> 03:27.832
That crazy bastard has a gun.

03:42.472 --> 03:44.015
Fuck this shit!

03:48.186 --> 03:49.562
Help me!

03:55.818 --> 03:56.694
Put the gun down!

03:59.864 --> 04:00.990
I said put it down!

04:09.249 --> 04:10.833
Please spare me.

04:10.917 --> 04:11.918
Put the gun down!

04:13.211 --> 04:16.005
Please show mercy, just this once!

04:20.134 --> 04:22.929
But how did you know
this chaos was coming, Mr. Wang?

04:23.513 --> 04:26.266
None of your business.
Just focus on the shot.

04:30.937 --> 04:32.188
Get that shot over there.

04:41.489 --> 04:42.740
Wait, one moment.

04:45.910 --> 04:47.704
I'm Officer Lee Do from Domyeong.

04:48.705 --> 04:50.039
Let me try talking to him.

04:54.877 --> 04:55.795
Do.

04:59.299 --> 05:00.300
Captain.

05:02.093 --> 05:03.428
Don't come any closer.

05:13.771 --> 05:16.357
You know better than anyone

05:17.942 --> 05:19.777
that this won't bring Se-yeong back.

05:28.036 --> 05:29.245
So put the gun down.

05:30.788 --> 05:33.333
Yeah, I thought
I knew that better than anyone.

05:38.671 --> 05:44.635
I believed that arresting scumbags
like him over and over until the end…

05:46.971 --> 05:50.141
would bring justice to the victims
who were wronged.

05:52.393 --> 05:54.645
You've been doing it so well until now.

06:00.193 --> 06:01.027
No.

06:02.153 --> 06:03.529
I actually didn't know.

06:06.324 --> 06:08.868
I didn't know anything at all.

06:16.000 --> 06:18.044
Now I can finally see reality
for what it is.

06:18.544 --> 06:20.963
What the fuck are you people doing?

06:22.131 --> 06:25.051
Don't just stand there and watch. Help me!

06:32.433 --> 06:34.227
Hold your fire.

06:35.228 --> 06:37.480
This is the limit of the law and of us.

06:39.273 --> 06:40.817
The law can't do anything.

06:45.488 --> 06:46.614
I'm sorry.

06:47.740 --> 06:49.534
But I've made up my mind now.

06:51.160 --> 06:52.829
Don't let that feeling fool you.

06:53.788 --> 06:55.498
When I first picked up a gun,

06:57.041 --> 06:58.835
do you remember…

07:01.629 --> 07:02.755
what you told me?

07:03.506 --> 07:04.340
Do.

07:07.885 --> 07:11.055
All of us adults here

07:12.432 --> 07:15.643
will make sure that bad man gets punished.

07:16.227 --> 07:17.437
My mom,

07:18.187 --> 07:19.313
dad,

07:20.231 --> 07:22.775
and little brother
were all brutally killed,

07:23.526 --> 07:26.863
but that man is happily
stuffing his face with bread.

07:27.363 --> 07:28.906
This is wrong!

07:29.740 --> 07:31.367
Yes, this is wrong.

07:31.451 --> 07:33.202
You're right about everything.

07:33.286 --> 07:34.245
But

07:35.538 --> 07:37.457
if you shoot that gun right now…

07:39.625 --> 07:42.920
it's only going to make his life easier.

07:44.255 --> 07:48.050
You know, scumbags like him
should be sent to prison

07:48.134 --> 07:50.928
to be punished for their deeds
for the rest of their lives.

07:51.512 --> 07:52.513
No.

07:54.348 --> 07:56.100
I don't think I'll be satisfied

07:57.393 --> 07:59.228
unless I pull the trigger.

07:59.896 --> 08:02.899
Don't let that feeling fool you.
None of it is real.

08:03.858 --> 08:06.235
The satisfaction will only last
for a moment.

08:08.070 --> 08:10.072
Killing a bad person…

08:13.075 --> 08:15.286
is the right thing to do, isn't it?

08:19.123 --> 08:20.666
Say you kill him.

08:22.084 --> 08:23.461
What about your future?

08:24.212 --> 08:26.923
You'll end up ruining your entire life.

08:30.009 --> 08:31.761
So just trust me this once.

08:31.844 --> 08:33.221
I promise.

08:33.930 --> 08:38.351
I will prove to you that not shooting him
was the right thing to do later.

08:38.851 --> 08:39.852
So, Do…

08:41.854 --> 08:45.233
Come on, Do.
Please put the gun down, okay? Please.

08:49.153 --> 08:52.615
In the end, all we could do
was send him to prison.

08:53.866 --> 08:55.535
Why does that matter?

08:58.621 --> 09:01.332
Thanks to you, Captain,
I've kept my life together.

09:03.501 --> 09:05.545
If something happened to you as well…

09:07.755 --> 09:09.173
how would I go on?

09:10.716 --> 09:13.970
Anyway, are you not taking
the promotion exam again?

09:15.263 --> 09:17.765
I'm happy and comfortable where I am.

09:17.848 --> 09:18.849
Look.

09:19.934 --> 09:22.645
With your age,
skills, experience, and abilities,

09:22.728 --> 09:25.314
not to mention your solid build
and good looks,

09:25.815 --> 09:28.568
you should've been a sergeant long ago,
if not higher.

09:30.069 --> 09:32.697
You fought so hard
just to never pick up a gun again.

09:32.780 --> 09:35.157
Where the hell are these guns coming from?

09:40.788 --> 09:43.624
Don't jump in
and get yourself involved, all right?

09:44.875 --> 09:47.420
I can't bear to see you get hurt.

09:48.087 --> 09:49.463
Physically or mentally.

09:50.881 --> 09:52.216
I'm begging you.

09:54.302 --> 09:55.303
Give me

09:56.887 --> 09:57.722
the gun.

10:13.571 --> 10:14.572
Do.

10:18.284 --> 10:19.535
How did you

10:21.287 --> 10:24.165
bear this pain at such a young age?

10:29.003 --> 10:30.838
It was all thanks to you, Captain.

10:32.965 --> 10:36.677
EXCLUSIVE: SHOTS FIRED AT BAR IN GYEONGIN
POLICE IN STANDOFF WITH SUSPECT

10:40.431 --> 10:42.433
This isn't what I had in mind.

11:09.835 --> 11:11.962
Come here. Shoot from this angle.

11:18.344 --> 11:19.762
Hey, Lee Do!

11:30.606 --> 11:33.359
Lee Do!

12:30.708 --> 12:31.542
Do.

12:37.423 --> 12:38.424
I'm sorry…

12:40.760 --> 12:41.594
Captain!

13:49.203 --> 13:52.373
You did well.

13:57.962 --> 13:59.421
The grown-ups are sorry.

14:02.675 --> 14:03.884
I'm sorry, Do.

14:21.861 --> 14:22.862
Let's head outside.

14:22.945 --> 14:23.779
What?

14:24.321 --> 14:26.490
We can't go out there.
That guy's got a gun.

14:27.157 --> 14:28.617
You damn coward.

14:28.701 --> 14:30.411
Hey, give me the camera!

14:54.393 --> 14:58.063
Do you remember how many people
you've killed by pulling the trigger?

14:59.815 --> 15:00.774
I mean…

15:02.276 --> 15:05.279
I heard you spared no one as a mercenary,
adult or child.

15:07.740 --> 15:08.824
But now,

15:10.326 --> 15:11.869
you kill some

15:12.995 --> 15:14.455
and save others.

15:18.626 --> 15:20.628
Is that your definition of justice?

15:22.755 --> 15:27.968
This is what you get
when you… straddle the line.

15:34.391 --> 15:35.517
You disgust me.

15:36.852 --> 15:37.770
Lee Do.

15:46.070 --> 15:46.904
Well…

15:49.490 --> 15:51.492
at least you were entertaining.

15:58.540 --> 15:59.625
Just wait and see.

16:01.627 --> 16:03.754
You'll wake up to a whole new world.

16:19.853 --> 16:21.063
Are you filming now?

16:21.146 --> 16:23.148
Yeah, it's coming out fine.

16:25.192 --> 16:27.987
I am Moon Baek,

16:29.488 --> 16:31.865
the mastermind
behind all the recent shootings.

16:34.868 --> 16:39.164
As you can see,
South Korea is no longer safe from guns.

16:39.248 --> 16:40.332
So I have…

16:40.833 --> 16:41.834
What's that?

16:41.917 --> 16:43.460
…prepared a gift.

16:44.086 --> 16:45.004
Starting now…

16:45.087 --> 16:46.046
EXCLUSIVE BREAKING NEWS

16:46.130 --> 16:50.175
…regardless of age, gender,
occupation, or nationality,

16:50.884 --> 16:53.178
if you want a gun, I'll give you one

16:54.179 --> 16:57.975
with no restrictions or conditions.

17:02.521 --> 17:04.064
Let me repeat that.

17:04.148 --> 17:07.943
Regardless of age, gender,
occupation, or nationality,

17:08.569 --> 17:11.030
if you want a gun, I'll give you one…

17:14.450 --> 17:17.911
with no restrictions or conditions.

17:18.912 --> 17:20.330
I'm not forcing anyone.

17:20.831 --> 17:24.376
All I want is to give you the power
to protect yourself.

17:24.460 --> 17:26.628
Why don't you do your job as a manager?

17:32.676 --> 17:33.594
"Gun."

17:44.354 --> 17:45.773
Hold him tighter.

17:46.440 --> 17:49.068
His pulse is dropping.
We need to stop the bleeding first.

17:49.151 --> 17:51.653
- Compression gauze, please.
- Here.

18:01.705 --> 18:03.457
Please move. We're in a hurry!

18:05.709 --> 18:06.710
Bed four.

18:08.045 --> 18:09.713
On three. One, two, three.

18:12.257 --> 18:13.842
- A gunshot victim?
- Yes.

18:14.927 --> 18:17.387
- Check vitals and prep for transfusion.
- Yes, Doctor.

18:19.223 --> 18:20.182
Just wait and see.

18:22.601 --> 18:24.728
You'll wake up to a whole new world.

18:50.963 --> 18:52.965
GYEONGIN EXPRESS

19:14.486 --> 19:16.363
It's here! I finally got the gun.

19:16.446 --> 19:19.032
South Korea is now a place
where guns get delivered.

19:19.116 --> 19:21.743
A shocking incident took place in Korea,

19:21.827 --> 19:25.372
where a police officer was shot
by a gun-trafficking organization.

19:25.455 --> 19:28.625
Let's aim to hit 30 million won
in Super Chats today.

19:28.709 --> 19:30.043
HE REALLY GOT A GUN

19:30.127 --> 19:32.921
I truly hope Officer Lee wakes up

19:33.422 --> 19:36.341
as soon as possible.

19:43.432 --> 19:46.351
Unidentified packages
with firearms and ammunition

19:46.435 --> 19:48.270
are being shipped nationwide.

19:48.937 --> 19:50.772
Authorities are on high alert,

19:50.856 --> 19:53.358
fearing that firearm distribution
via courier services

19:53.442 --> 19:55.402
could lead to an active shooting.

19:55.485 --> 19:58.071
Even martial law
wouldn't be enough right now.

19:58.155 --> 20:00.282
No, it's still too early to judge.

20:00.365 --> 20:02.367
How can you say that
after what's happened?

20:02.451 --> 20:04.703
Our priority is
accurate situation assessment.

20:04.786 --> 20:07.331
Given the defendant's intoxication,

20:07.831 --> 20:10.584
first-time offense, and remorse,

20:11.210 --> 20:13.462
I sentence them
to three years in prison and--

20:13.545 --> 20:15.964
- I object.
- Excuse me?

20:16.048 --> 20:20.302
I will personally carry out
his execution here and now.

20:24.014 --> 20:25.807
This is seriously amazing.

20:25.891 --> 20:27.309
You don't need a real gun.

20:27.392 --> 20:29.519
Look, this looks just like a real gun.

20:29.603 --> 20:32.773
With modifications,
an air gun can be deadlier than a firearm.

20:32.856 --> 20:38.737
The random spread of guns has fueled fears
that anyone could be armed,

20:39.488 --> 20:43.450
driving crowds to buy firearms blindly.

20:43.533 --> 20:47.287
A nostalgic M16 costs only 20,000 won.

20:47.371 --> 20:49.081
- Give me one first.
- I'll buy one too.

20:52.167 --> 20:53.710
Give me a sec, all right?

20:53.794 --> 20:56.922
Long-suppressed sociopathic tendencies

20:57.756 --> 21:01.134
are now being triggered by these guns.

21:01.760 --> 21:03.262
The real problem

21:03.845 --> 21:05.222
is that this anxiety

21:06.056 --> 21:08.016
is more contagious than expected.

21:08.100 --> 21:11.395
Didn't I tell you
to submit the report before leaving?

21:11.478 --> 21:16.316
Sir, I've worked nights for three weeks,
and it's my daughter's birthday today.

21:16.400 --> 21:19.403
You think you're the only one
with a family and a daughter?

21:19.486 --> 21:21.446
Why don't you just quit your job?

21:21.530 --> 21:22.614
Understood, sir.

21:23.156 --> 21:26.410
I'll bring her a birthday cake,
then head back to the office.

21:27.577 --> 21:29.663
Damn, if only I could kill this bastard.

21:38.422 --> 21:39.881
- Hey, welcome home.
- Daddy!

21:39.965 --> 21:40.799
Yes?

21:40.882 --> 21:42.926
This looks like a real gun.

21:47.889 --> 21:50.392
GYEONGIN UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

22:01.987 --> 22:06.825
Recent shootings
are fueling anxiety among citizens.

22:06.908 --> 22:09.953
Many are avoiding going out
for routine tasks, and…

22:13.123 --> 22:14.249
Yes, Mr. President.

22:17.002 --> 22:18.378
Noted, Mr. President.

22:18.462 --> 22:20.005
I will relay the message.

22:26.345 --> 22:28.263
We're now declaring a national emergency.

22:30.849 --> 22:34.269
There has never been
a time of greater conflict in history.

22:34.353 --> 22:36.271
Do you remember
the early days of COVID-19?

22:36.772 --> 22:39.858
It only took three days
for masks to sell out nationwide.

22:39.941 --> 22:44.905
Who would just sit back and watch
as guns spread across the nation?

22:44.988 --> 22:49.534
While you two were speaking,
a shocking poll result came in.

22:49.618 --> 22:55.540
Over 40% said that gun ownership
should be legalized in Korea.

22:56.041 --> 22:58.919
Including conditional permits,
the majority supports it.

23:01.171 --> 23:03.507
The number of packages collected
is too low.

23:03.590 --> 23:05.926
Four million packages
are distributed daily.

23:06.009 --> 23:08.553
We can't possibly manage it this way.

23:08.637 --> 23:12.557
South Korea, once drug-free,
is now a place

23:12.641 --> 23:17.187
where drugs are accessible
anytime, anywhere.

23:17.270 --> 23:19.898
Would it be any different for guns?

23:19.981 --> 23:23.443
The emergence
of firearms of unknown origin

23:23.527 --> 23:26.822
is bringing significant changes
to our society.

23:26.905 --> 23:30.659
What is your opinion
on legalizing gun ownership?

23:30.742 --> 23:32.244
Please sign our petition.

23:37.416 --> 23:38.625
Say no to guns!

23:38.708 --> 23:40.710
"Say no"? Come on, man.

23:40.794 --> 23:44.840
This country had knife attacks in daylight
even before we had guns.

23:44.923 --> 23:48.718
Now those lunatics will bring guns
to schools, hospitals, and day cares.

23:48.802 --> 23:52.055
By that logic, even school teachers
and doctors should be carrying guns.

23:52.139 --> 23:54.099
- You call that a country?
- That's right!

23:54.182 --> 23:59.354
People like you, who incite gun violence,
should be locked up immediately.

23:59.438 --> 24:01.565
What if our kids get shot by those guns?

24:01.648 --> 24:03.942
To protect your kids,
we need guns even more.

24:04.025 --> 24:04.860
Exactly!

24:04.943 --> 24:08.947
If we all have guns,
they'll be too afraid to pull out theirs.

24:09.030 --> 24:10.407
Don't be ridiculous!

24:10.490 --> 24:13.076
- How is that ridiculous?
- Have you lost your mind?

24:15.662 --> 24:20.375
The empty streets
are filling up with protesters.

24:20.459 --> 24:24.337
The widespread public fear of guns
is taking a new turn.

24:25.088 --> 24:28.216
All shipped items were delivered
without any issues.

24:30.802 --> 24:31.803
Get ready

24:33.096 --> 24:34.181
for the next step.

24:40.187 --> 24:42.189
Are you feeling any discomfort?

24:42.272 --> 24:43.732
No, I'm fine.

24:51.948 --> 24:54.743
- I'll see you at your afternoon checkup.
- Okay.

25:00.123 --> 25:01.291
Finish these tonight.

25:01.374 --> 25:03.460
We have the head nurse's evaluation
next week.

25:03.543 --> 25:06.880
We don't want any issues with our team,
so finish everything today.

25:07.714 --> 25:10.842
But this is just too much.

25:11.510 --> 25:13.094
I'm on the night shift again today.

25:13.595 --> 25:14.721
So what?

25:15.514 --> 25:17.474
You're talking back to me now, huh?

25:18.099 --> 25:19.768
And that's hardly anything.

25:19.851 --> 25:21.978
It's only hard
because you're so damn slow.

25:23.438 --> 25:24.523
Okay, I'll do it.

26:01.017 --> 26:03.728
We're at each other's throats
every chance we get,

26:03.812 --> 26:05.772
so why have we been meeting
so often lately?

26:06.690 --> 26:08.316
We might become too close.

26:08.400 --> 26:11.278
Hey, you came here
for the same reason we did,

26:11.361 --> 26:14.155
so how about you shut that mouth of yours?

26:15.740 --> 26:17.576
The world's changing.

26:18.618 --> 26:21.246
How can we sit still? We must change too.

26:21.997 --> 26:24.249
If we don't want to get shot
and killed like Gong.

26:24.332 --> 26:26.418
- Are we at a funeral?
- Who's that?

26:27.460 --> 26:28.878
Why the gloomy vibe?

26:28.962 --> 26:31.881
Didn't you come to buy guns?
If not, I'll just leave.

26:32.465 --> 26:34.759
Is this for fucking real?

26:35.260 --> 26:39.389
Hey, you little shit. How old are you?

26:39.472 --> 26:42.058
You little punk,
how dare you walk in like you own--

26:46.187 --> 26:49.566
Does being older give you
a free pass to everything in this country?

26:50.066 --> 26:53.862
Why does everyone look so shocked?
Never seen someone die before?

26:55.238 --> 26:58.283
If you're all done gawking,
pay attention to me.

26:58.366 --> 27:00.660
Stay focused and get serious.

27:00.744 --> 27:03.038
I'm looking for a new partner,

27:03.121 --> 27:05.415
but too many cooks spoil the broth.

27:05.498 --> 27:06.541
I only want one.

27:11.296 --> 27:13.465
Whoever shoots me with that gun.

27:13.548 --> 27:15.634
First come, first served. Just one.

27:20.096 --> 27:23.266
Stay the fuck where you are.

27:26.811 --> 27:29.105
It's probably easier to use than a knife.

27:31.149 --> 27:32.150
Shoot me.

27:32.651 --> 27:34.611
You think we're fucking stupid?

27:35.111 --> 27:37.489
You think I won't shoot, you motherfucker?

27:37.989 --> 27:38.865
Shoot me already.

27:38.948 --> 27:41.868
You fucking piece of shit.
Fuck you, motherfucker!

28:19.739 --> 28:20.865
Did that scare you?

28:25.203 --> 28:26.621
Be sure to answer my calls.

28:27.664 --> 28:28.498
I will.

28:29.916 --> 28:30.917
And clean this up.

28:40.218 --> 28:43.138
GYEONGIN UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

29:02.741 --> 29:05.452
Officially, you've taken down 99 targets.

29:06.035 --> 29:07.996
As of today, the count is 100.

29:08.079 --> 29:11.291
You just wanted to shoot them all down,
didn't you?

29:15.420 --> 29:16.629
And at 27 Baekju-ro,

29:17.505 --> 29:20.008
there's someone about to pull the trigger.

29:20.508 --> 29:21.801
Lee Do!

29:55.168 --> 29:56.252
You're awake.

29:59.714 --> 30:02.050
You shouldn't move. You need to rest.

30:03.384 --> 30:04.886
Where's my captain?

30:04.969 --> 30:05.970
You shouldn't.

30:07.013 --> 30:09.599
Please calm down.

30:10.183 --> 30:12.352
- You shouldn't be standing.
- My captain.

30:12.852 --> 30:15.146
- Please stay put.
- Please find my captain.

30:15.230 --> 30:17.148
- Please.
- His name is Jo Hyeon-sik.

30:17.232 --> 30:18.149
Calm down.

30:18.650 --> 30:19.734
- Please.
- I…

30:22.278 --> 30:23.780
- Are you okay?
- Are you okay?

30:23.863 --> 30:25.490
Where is my captain?

30:25.573 --> 30:27.784
Calm down, please!

30:27.867 --> 30:29.285
Where's Jo Hyeon-sik?

30:29.369 --> 30:31.120
- One moment.
- Excuse me. My captain…

30:31.204 --> 30:33.039
- Please relax.
- Has anybody seen him?

30:33.122 --> 30:36.125
Please tell me where Jo Hyeon-sik is.
He's my captain.

30:36.709 --> 30:38.378
- I…
- Officer Lee.

35:19.617 --> 35:24.622
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang
